  "borough": "Ealing",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - On 5 September 2025, the existing house's previous change of use from a Dwellinghouse (Use Class C3) to a House in Multiple Occupation (Sui Generis) occupied by up to seven persons was not lawful within the meaning of Section 191 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended) by reason of:\r\n\r\nThe applicant's submitted evidence demonstrating that, on the balance of probabilities, the existing house was used for a purpose not within its existing use class but instead as a House in Multiple Occupation (Sui Generis) occupied by seven persons, as specified by Article 3, Clause 3 (1A) and Schedule 1, Part C, Class C4 of the Town and Country Planning (Use Classes) Order 1987 (as amended);\r\n\r\nThe permitted development rights which previously applied to the house in accordance with Schedule 2, Part 3, Class L of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended) prior to the commencement of an Article 4 Direction of 4 September 2023 not being relevant to assessing the lawfulness of its use as a House in Multiple Occupation (Sui Generis) occupied by seven persons and;\r\n\r\nThe existing house's change of use to a House in Multiple Occupation (Sui Generis) occupied by seven persons therefore being development requiring and not having been grated planning permission, as specified by Section 55 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended), and not being lawful.  "
  ],
